{
    "article_summary": "This study describes a protecting group-free photocatalyzed O-arylation of quinic acid (QA) and its tetraacetyl derivative (TAQA) using aryl halides. The reaction utilizes a dual catalytic system consisting of an organic photocatalyst (5CzBN) and a nickel complex (NiCl2\u00b7glyme/dtbbpy) under visible light irradiation. The method selectively forms O-aryl esters without decarboxylation or lactonization, and computational studies suggest an energy transfer mechanism from the excited photocatalyst to the Ni(II) species to facilitate reductive elimination.",
